for s,b,a,r in [(44,'For heroes have the whole earth as their tomb; and in lands far from their own, where the column with its epitaph proclaims it, there is enshrined in every breast a record unwritten, with no tablet to preserve it but that of the heart.','For distinguished men have the whole earth as their tomb. It is not only inscriptions on monuments in their own country that commemorate them: even in foreign lands an unwritten memory lives in each person’s heart, a memory of their spirit more than of their deeds.','Greek2.43 οὐ στηλῶν μόνον ἐν τῇ οἰκείᾳ ... ἀλλὰ καὶ ἐν τῇ μὴ προσηκούσῃ: printed Crawley conflates home/foreign and omits spirit/deed contrast.'),(45,'but fortunate indeed are those who draw for their lot a death so glorious as the one that has caused your mourning, and to whom life has been so exactly measured that it ends in the happiness in which it was passed.','but fortunate are those whose lot is most honourable: theirs is an honourable death, and yours an honourable grief. Fortunate too are those whose lives are so measured that their happiness lasts until death.','Greek2.44 explicitly pairs their death with parents’ grief; restore omitted counterpart.'),(45,'since no fair or just policy can be expected of the citizen who does not, like his fellows, bring to the decision the interests and apprehensions of a father.','since no one can deliberate fairly or justly unless, like the others, he also puts his own children at risk.','Greek2.44 specifically equal risk to children, not simply parental interests.'),(46,'if I must say anything to those of you who will now be in widowhood','if I must say anything about women’s virtue to those of you who will now be widows','Restore omitted subject female excellence; preserve historical speaker’s claim.'),(48,'“And now that you have made an end of your lamentations for your relatives, you may depart.”','“Now mourn each for your own relatives, and then depart.”','Greek2.46 ἀπολοφυράμενοι ... ἄπιτε instructs mourning then departure, not claim mourning already complete.')]:x.append(dict(language='modern-en',chapter=6,slot=s,before=b,after=a,reason=r))
(p/'edits-006i.json').write_text(json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
